# ============================================================================
# Build context for src/CoupleOS.Api/Dockerfile.
#
# Two jobs, and the first one is not about image size.
#
# `bin/` and `obj/` hold a restore graph resolved on the *host*. On Windows
# that graph carries C:\Users\...\.nuget paths and win-x64 assets, and copying
# it into a Linux build makes `dotnet publish` resolve against paths that do
# not exist — a failure whose message points at NuGet rather than at this file.
# The build must restore from scratch inside the container.
#
# `.env` and `appsettings.Development.json` are gitignored, so they exist on a
# developer's machine and not in a clean clone. Excluding them here means the
# image built locally is the image built from a clean clone, and no secret is
# ever baked into a layer. Configuration reaches the container through compose
# environment variables instead.
# ============================================================================

# --- Host build output: correctness, not size ------------------------------
**/bin/
**/obj/

# --- Secrets and machine-local configuration -------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/appsettings.Development.json
**/appsettings.Local.json
**/secrets.json
*.pem
*.key

# --- Not part of the application -------------------------------------------
# src/ has no runtime dependency on any of these; the only mentions of `data/`
# inside src/ are comments citing schema.sql. The db service mounts data/ from
# the host, so the api image has no reason to carry it.
.git
.gitattributes
.gitignore
.github
.serena
.vs
.vscode
.idea
tests/
data/
docs/
decisions/
design/
product/
research/
assets/
README.md
docker-compose.yml
.dockerignore
